<title>BELGIUM: Exceptionals boost City Hotels profit.</title>
<headline>Exceptionals boost City Hotels profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		    729.45   vs    20.79</p>
<p>    Current net loss		     19.31   vs    38.32 profit</p>
<p>    Net dividend per share (francs) 192	vs    42</p>
<p>NOTE - City Hotels said in a statement the &quot;spectacular&quot; rise of net profit reflected important capital gains. It said it made a net capital gain of 682 million francs on the sale of 90 percent in EuroBelgian Airlines (EBA) to Richard Branson's Virgin and a net capital gain of 65 million francs on the sale of the Hampton Inn hotel in Baltimore, U.S.  </p>
<p>    Cons turnover		     1,679.80   vs 6,174.42</p>
<p>    Current net cash-flow	     436.17   vs   692.27</p>
<p>NOTE - City Hotels said the dividend rise reflected the rise of earnings linked to the sale of EBA.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
